@startuml sequence_audit_request
!theme plain
autonumber
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 15

title Sequence Diagram: Frontend Requesting Repo Audit

actor "User" as User
participant "React Frontend\n(Live Demo View)" as Frontend
participant "FastAPI Engine\n(/api/audit)" as Backend
participant "Pandas Engine\n(Statistical Model)" as Engine

User -> Frontend : Enter Repo URL / Identifier (e.g., 'fastapi/fastapi')
User -> Frontend : Click "Run Audit" button
activate Frontend

Frontend -> Frontend : Set UI state: isLoading = true\nDisplay loading spinner & disable button

Frontend -> Backend : GET /api/audit?owner={owner}&repo={repo}
activate Backend

Backend -> Backend : Validate query parameters (owner, repo)
Backend -> Engine : Trigger audit analysis pipeline
activate Engine

Engine --> Backend : Return computed payload\n(medians, 90% CI, flagged anomalies)
deactivate Engine

Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK JSON Response\n{total_closed_prs, baseline_medians, anomalies: [...]}
deactivate Backend

Frontend -> Frontend : Set UI state: isLoading = false\nStore audit results in component state
Frontend -> Frontend : Render Baseline Metrics Cards\n(Small, Medium, Large medians)
Frontend -> Frontend : Render Flagged Anomalies Table\n(PR #, Author, Review Time, CI bounds)

Frontend --> User : Present Interactive Audit Results & Anomaly Badges
deactivate Frontend

@enduml
